  "description": "Event encoding and content hash (BATCH-003, BATCH-004, BATCH-006). `event` is the logical event; bytes inside it are {\"$hex\": ...}. `encoded_hex` is the msgpack the Rust producer emits for it (lowercase hex). `content_hash_hex` = sha256(encoded bytes). `state_from_zero_hex` = sha256(32 zero bytes || content hash), the chain state after this one event. Cases without `event` are raw byte strings. Floats in `risk`, `skin_detection` and `nsfw_detection` are stored as msgpack float32; a consumer sees the float32 value widened to a double."
